# PHASE 5 — FOUNDER-CONTROLLED STAFF ONBOARDING

The staff system is particularly important.

I want to control who becomes a member of the ASKIA MARKET team.

A person must not become staff merely by registering, selecting a staff role or entering a staff email address.

## Staff application and invitation

Support two secure workflows:

### Workflow A — Founder creates or invites staff

1. I open the private Super Admin dashboard.
2. I select Staff Management.
3. I invite a person using their email address.
4. I assign their job title, role and permissions.
5. The person receives an invitation through a configured secure mechanism.
6. They verify their email and establish their own account.
7. The server activates only the permissions I authorized.

### Workflow B — Someone requests staff access

1. A person can submit a staff-access request if this feature is enabled.
2. The request remains pending.
3. They cannot enter the staff dashboard or use staff APIs.
4. I review the application in the Super Admin dashboard.
5. I may approve, reject or request further information.
6. If approved, I explicitly assign a job title, role and permissions.
7. Only then can the server activate their staff access.

A pending staff applicant must not be treated as an active staff member.

Never grant staff access based on a client-supplied role, email address or registration form.

## Staff management capabilities

The founder must be able to:

- Add or invite staff.
- Approve or reject staff applications.
- Assign job titles and departments.
- Assign predefined or custom roles.
- Grant and revoke granular permissions.
- Edit staff positions.
- Suspend or reactivate staff.
- Remove staff access.
- Review active and pending staff.
- View appropriate account activity and audit records.
- Revoke sessions when staff access is suspended or removed.
- Prevent staff from promoting themselves.
- Prevent staff from changing founder permissions or assigning themselves Super Admin.
- Prevent unauthorized users from editing the staff roster or granting privileges.

The founder should be able to add new positions and remove obsolete positions without manually changing frontend code. Removing a role must not silently transfer its permissions to another role.

Before removing a role that is still assigned to people, require a safe reassignment or revocation process.

